nt factors in the  movie the film stalock and cast includes  Mexican actor Mabel Karena who plays no  More's cousin and Venezuelan actor Alex  livinali is the warrior atuma  tenochuerta even learned the Mayan  language Mabel Cadena was positively  overwhelmed by the indigenous  representation this movie fought for to  me it's crazy because I can find in the  movie the little things from my Mexican  culture number five some of the most  intense underwater training imaginable  the actors spent eight hours filming a  day in a large water tank they trained  with Colombian national record holder  Alex linas an instructor with free  diving instructors International Alex  livinale explained we trained for months  the first time I was there for like 30  seconds but as the time went on I was  there for like three minutes relaxing  number six  Leticia Wright had a special bond with  Chadwick Boseman Leticia was Chadwick's  favorite doctor to work with so Ryan  coogler knew that in order to honor him  it would be important to elevate her  character one of the things Ryan took  note of was Chad's smile off camera as  himself his smile was huge like a  Cheshire Cat but when he was on screen  his demeanor was a lot more serious she  was the only actor who would get who  would get him the small ass child on  South Side man he broke character number  seven intense action movies can make for  some pretty scary stunt work Leticia  Wright suffered a pretty severe injury  involving a motorcycle  it's centered to the hospital with a  fractured shoulder and a concussion she  was shooting a chase scene that put her  on a biscuit rig which allowed the  camera to shoot her while riding in a  real environment the rig ended up  clipping a median and it shifted the  bike off causing it to take a pretty  severe tumble with Leticia still on it  she told variety I'm still processing it  I'm still working through it in therapy  it was really traumatic production had  to be paused for two months while she  recovered number eight not the most  common thing to design costume designer  Ruth e Carter had to do extensive tests  on the costumes designed for the movie  in order to make sure they would hold up  and retain form underwater the team had  never worked with underwater costumes  before so this posed a whole new set of  challenges for the water scenes we had a  20-foot tank in which we did tests  divers went down in the water and I had  to put them in costumes that included  headdresses and capes just to see what  those costumes would do in the water and  I ended up putting weights in number  nine did you notice shuri's Adidas  they were actually Hollow and made from  a new 4D technology the company is  launching soon at first they only sent  them one sneaker but they ended up  convincing Adidas to create enough shoes  for the motorcycle stunt when you go  outside of our industry they're going  what do you mean you need two two we  need two we need ten  number 10 rewriting a script without  your main character is no easy task the  script for wakanda forever was already  completed when Chadwick Boseman passed  away so unfortunately they were forced  to create a totally different story Ryan  coogler thanks his phenomenal team when  it came to recreating the story in honor  of Chad when making the first film the  bond they developed was really that of a  family so Ryan knew exactly how to write  everyone's motivations and voices I had  a good idea of what folks would be  willing to do and not willing to do  these all very strong  minded people when it came down to it he  really just wanted to honor Chad as well  as keeping the Integrity of the film  whether it was a journey of of grief and  loss that we were navigating as we as we  did this to honor our brother number 11  the music in this film speaks volumes  the task was to find an artist that  could meet them thematically where the  film was at enter Rihanna Ryan thought  that because Rihanna had had recently  become a mother she would actually be  more inclined to create a track for the  film motherhood is a massive theme and  Motif in this in this film and it was  incredible at the timed out multiple  people from all over the world  contributed to this song including tens  an artist from Nigeria Rihanna put our  touch on it and we finally heard it I  was moved and then she said y'all did it  for Chad number 12. the crew really did  their research the wakandans wearing  white to King t'challa's funeral is  based on Ghanaian tradition when  designing the hundreds of funeral  costumes Ruth e Carter ended up taking  inspiration from several cultures  throughout Africa to create a unique  identity for each wakandan tribe you  could actually identify all the tribes  even though they were all in white but  the white unified them in tribute to the  Ascension of Chadwick Boseman  number 13. there are only a few things  Ryan coogler shares in the early  versions of the script before Chadwick  boseman's passing King t'challa was in  mourning for the time he lost between  Avengers Infinity war and Avengers end  game one of the big themes in the script  was grief which is still a huge theme of  the current film but in a different way  Ryan coogler talked to inverse about his  thought process the character was going  to be grieving the loss of time you know  coming back after being gone for five  years  as a man with so much responsibility to  so many coming back after a forced  five-year absence that's what the film  was tackling number 14 the water posed a  major challenge for this cast most of  the cast was not comfortable in the  water Ryan coogler explains the sphere  of water as one of the impositions of  Black Culture a lot of us have we're  ready to have fear of water you know I  myself had the same thing going on most  everyone in the cast including Ryan had  to learn how to swim or at least improve  their swimming skills Lupita Nyong'o  actually took it upon herself to 